      "problem": "Solve the inequality ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14227573/assets/2abe9cdeada000e13f085d8be9750f26a184e68557283f1bdec4e003afabf173.svg)",
      "worked_solution": "First, we isolate the exponential term:\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14227573/assets/c7b01893901c216f2285f49c2fb38819dc193d003881b4e5719867f9c1863844.svg)\n\nNext, recall that a positive number raised to any real power is always positive. Since ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14227573/assets/e19edf5f19279dad194a5f66ac4979df2518fedd68e0f768877ee0b5024b3540.svg) we have\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14227573/assets/864dbe8402aa67932c2fcb31f22012c4904f575976d1fc62b027bb84443b6c3f.svg)\nfor every real value of ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14227573/assets/cff7b257e3c71ec70dc7cd273bdd1cced4254993a43cffbfc338460c21bc7319.svg)\n\nIn particular, every value of ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14227573/assets/69e8d1fbd034994ec8c4d373a6428eb5f0344c0c9d71f7c624525b550fa73fdb.svg) is greater than ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14227573/assets/2ed49f2115a6860b40a8ea69b5672921fb832f8592a69969e4c9f4bb370c1aa6.svg) Therefore,\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14227573/assets/2f954e20489fbbbc6b2a5e7a577ab39e8f4ea3769202c1db83c2db99549caec0.svg)\nfor all real values of ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14227573/assets/cff7b257e3c71ec70dc7cd273bdd1cced4254993a43cffbfc338460c21bc7319.svg)\n\nHence, the original inequality is satisfied for all real numbers.",
